# Jazz grooves.
#
# One block per groove:  [style kind intensity=low-high]
#   kind       verse, chorus or bridge (intro/outro play verse, solo/breakdown bridge)
#   intensity  the bar intensities (0-1) this groove suits; neighbours overlap on purpose
# Then one line per instrument:  <instrument>[@min complexity] <bar 1> | <bar 2> ...
#   instruments  K S RS SS H HO HP R RB C C2 CH SP T1 T2 T3 T4
#   steps        . rest   x hit   X accent   o soft   g ghost
#   a bar has 4, 8, 12, 16, 24 or 32 steps; spaces inside a bar are ignored
# Add a block to add a groove; the blocks of a style and kind are its variants,
# lightest first. A new style name makes a new style of this genre.
# Playable by one drummer: snare, crash and toms 1/3 right hand; hi-hat, ride,
# tom 2 left hand; kick and hi-hat pedal feet; at most 3 hits on one step.

[swing verse intensity=0.20-0.60]
R x.. x.x x.. x.x | x.. x.x x.. x.x
HP ... x.. ... x.. | ... x.. ... x..
K o.. o.. o.. o.. | o.. o.. o.. o..

